The invariant mass combination shown in figure 5.6 is calculated, and a \(D^{*\pm}\) candidate is identified when the invariant mass of a \(D^{0}\)-candidate + \(\pi\) (identified with the TPC) falls within the range \(M_{K\pi\pi_{s}}-M_{K\pi}=0.143-0.147\)GeV/c\({}^{2}\). When that condition is met, the \((\Delta\eta,\Delta\phi)\) ordered-pair is calculated for the \(D^{0}\)-candidate + \(\pi\) and is binned in a separate histogram. The set of \(\pi\) that satisfy this invariant mass condition are then referred to as \(\pi_{soft}\)

